# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Giving Hand — Web Platform (Vite + React) environment template
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values:
#     cp .env.example .env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase project credentials ─────────────────────────────
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then find these
# under Project Settings → API.
#
# IMPORTANT: as shipped, most of this app reads its Supabase URL
# and anon key directly from src/utils/supabaseClient.ts.
# If you want to run against YOUR OWN Supabase project, either:
#   1) paste your values into src/utils/supabaseClient.ts, or
#   2) set the variables below AND update the imports that point
#      at '@/config/supabaseClient' to read from env instead.

# Vite-style variables (documented in README):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# Legacy CRA-style names still referenced by src/config/supabaseClient.ts:
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
REACT_APP_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# ── Notes on safety ──────────────────────────────────────────
# • The "anon" key is a publishable key — safe for client code,
#   provided Row Level Security (RLS) is enabled on all tables.
# • NEVER put a service_role key in this file: it bypasses RLS
#   and must stay server-side only.
# • `.env` is git-ignored — never commit real secrets.
